   "source": [
    "# Exercise 1.6 — The distribution, as code\n",
    "\n",
    "Course: 02805 Social Graphs and Interactions (Fall 2026) — Week 1, \"Your toolbox\" / \"Degree distributions\"\n",
    "\n",
    "Rebuilds the two Week 1 explorables (the adjacency-matrix-style Marvel walkthrough and the real-degrees / two-distributions explorables) as real code, on the actual week-1 Marvel dataset from the [course data page](https://sunelehmann.com/socialgraphs2026-web/data/).\n",
    "\n",
    "Data files (`data/week1_nodes.tsv`, `data/week1_edges.tsv`) were downloaded from the course data page exactly as described there — the frozen 2026-08-26 snapshot of Wikipedia's *Category:Marvel Comics superheroes*, 303 characters, edges wherever one character's article links to another's."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a9b050f3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "a30d6570",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-03T14:51:48.821797Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-03T14:51:48.821532Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-03T14:51:51.223248Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-03T14:51:51.220943Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import networkx as nx\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.rcParams[\"figure.dpi\"] = 100\n",
    "RNG = np.random.default_rng(42)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "56c17c08",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Part 1 — Load the network\n",
    "\n",
    "Load `week1_nodes.tsv` / `week1_edges.tsv` exactly as the course data page instructs: add **every node first**, so the 17 isolated characters (no link in either direction) survive, then add the edges as a directed graph."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "f16ee136",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-03T14:51:51.226861Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-03T14:51:51.226470Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-03T14:51:51.301712Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-03T14:51:51.300042Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "n = 303 nodes, m = 1784 directed edges\n",
      "Matches the course page: n=303, 1,784 directed links. ✓\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "nodes = pd.read_csv(\"data/week1_nodes.tsv\", sep=\"\\t\", comment=\"#\", quoting=3)  # QUOTE_NONE\n",
    "edges = pd.read_csv(\"data/week1_edges.tsv\", sep=\"\\t\", comment=\"#\", names=[\"source\", \"target\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "G = nx.DiGraph()\n",
    "G.add_nodes_from(nodes.node_id)\n",
    "G.add_edges_from(edges.itertuples(index=False))\n",
    "\n",
    "n = G.number_of_nodes()\n",
    "m_directed = G.number_of_edges()\n",
    "print(f\"n = {n} nodes, m = {m_directed} directed edges\")\n",
    "\n",
    "assert n == 303, f\"expected 303 nodes, got {n}\"\n",
    "assert m_directed == 1784, f\"expected 1784 directed edges, got {m_directed}\"\n",
    "print(\"Matches the course page: n=303, 1,784 directed links. ✓\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "e898b5fa",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-03T14:51:51.305458Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-03T14:51:51.304929Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-03T14:51:51.322053Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-03T14:51:51.319570Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "undirected pairs m = 1434\n",
      "undirected average degree <k> = 2m/n = 9.47\n",
      "Matches the course page: m=1,434 pairs, <k> ≈ 9.5. ✓\n",
      "\n",
      "reciprocated pairs (A links B AND B links A): 350\n",
      "check: 1784 directed edges - 350 reciprocated pairs = 1434 = m_undirected? True\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Collapse to the undirected view: two characters are \"connected\" if either links the other.\n",
    "G_undirected = G.to_undirected()\n",
    "m_undirected = G_undirected.number_of_edges()\n",
    "avg_k_undirected = 2 * m_undirected / n\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"undirected pairs m = {m_undirected}\")\n",
    "print(f\"undirected average degree <k> = 2m/n = {avg_k_undirected:.2f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "assert m_undirected == 1434, f\"expected 1434 undirected pairs, got {m_undirected}\"\n",
    "assert abs(avg_k_undirected - 9.5) < 0.1\n",
    "print(\"Matches the course page: m=1,434 pairs, <k> ≈ 9.5. ✓\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Why do the two edge counts differ? Count reciprocated pairs directly, don't just assert the arithmetic.\n",
    "reciprocated_directed_edges = sum(1 for u, v in G.edges() if G.has_edge(v, u))\n",
    "reciprocated_pairs = reciprocated_directed_edges // 2\n",
    "print(f\"\\nreciprocated pairs (A links B AND B links A): {reciprocated_pairs}\")\n",
    "print(f\"check: {m_directed} directed edges - {reciprocated_pairs} reciprocated pairs \"\n",
    "      f\"= {m_directed - reciprocated_pairs} = m_undirected? {m_directed - reciprocated_pairs == m_undirected}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "990b9811",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Why the two counts differ, in one sentence:** every one of the 350 pairs of characters that link to each other in *both* directions contributes 2 directed edges but only 1 undirected edge, so those 700 directed edges collapse into 350 undirected ones, shrinking the total from 1,784 down to exactly 1,784 − 350 = 1,434 — matching the course page's own aside that \"350 of them link both ways.\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5aa0a036",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Part 2 — In-degree and out-degree distributions\n",
    "\n",
    "Reproduce the *real-degrees* explorable: in-degree and out-degree, each on linear and log–log axes, plotted against $k+1$ so the 17 zero-degree isolates survive the log axis (an axis of raw $k$ can't show a 0)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "070af86c",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-03T14:51:51.325910Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-03T14:51:51.325622Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-03T14:51:52.657000Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-03T14:51:52.654711Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1100x800 with 4 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "in_degree = dict(G.in_degree())\n",
    "out_degree = dict(G.out_degree())\n",
    "\n",
    "def degree_distribution(degree_dict, n):\n",
    "    \"\"\"u = k+1. Returns arrays (u, P(u)) with P(u) = (# nodes with that degree) / n,\n",
    "    keeping only u-values that actually occur (a log axis can't plot P=0 anyway).\"\"\"\n",
    "    u_values = np.array([k + 1 for k in degree_dict.values()])\n",
    "    u_max = u_values.max()\n",
    "    counts = np.bincount(u_values, minlength=u_max + 1)\n",
    "    u_all = np.arange(1, u_max + 1)\n",
    "    P_all = counts[1:] / n\n",
    "    mask = P_all > 0\n",
    "    return u_all[mask], P_all[mask]\n",
    "\n",
    "u_in, P_in = degree_distribution(in_degree, n)\n",
    "u_out, P_out = degree_distribution(out_degree, n)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(11, 8))\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[0, 0].bar(u_in, P_in, width=0.9, color=\"tab:red\")\n",
    "axes[0, 0].set_title(\"In-degree — linear axes\")\n",
    "axes[0, 0].set_xlabel(\"in-degree + 1\")\n",
    "axes[0, 0].set_ylabel(\"P(k)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[0, 1].scatter(u_in, P_in, s=15, color=\"tab:red\")\n",
    "axes[0, 1].set_xscale(\"log\"); axes[0, 1].set_yscale(\"log\")\n",
    "axes[0, 1].set_title(\"In-degree — log–log axes\")\n",
    "axes[0, 1].set_xlabel(\"in-degree + 1 (log)\")\n",
    "axes[0, 1].set_ylabel(\"P(k) (log)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[1, 0].bar(u_out, P_out, width=0.9, color=\"tab:blue\")\n",
    "axes[1, 0].set_title(\"Out-degree — linear axes\")\n",
    "axes[1, 0].set_xlabel(\"out-degree + 1\")\n",
    "axes[1, 0].set_ylabel(\"P(k)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[1, 1].scatter(u_out, P_out, s=15, color=\"tab:blue\")\n",
    "axes[1, 1].set_xscale(\"log\"); axes[1, 1].set_yscale(\"log\")\n",
    "axes[1, 1].set_title(\"Out-degree — log–log axes\")\n",
    "axes[1, 1].set_xlabel(\"out-degree + 1 (log)\")\n",
    "axes[1, 1].set_ylabel(\"P(k) (log)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "3560881a",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-03T14:51:52.660985Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-03T14:51:52.660599Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-03T14:51:52.670692Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-03T14:51:52.669407Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Top 5 by in-degree (most-linked-to — 'famous'):\n",
      "  Spider-Man                       in-degree = 106\n",
      "  Hulk                             in-degree = 64\n",
      "  Wolverine (character)            in-degree = 60\n",
      "  Doctor Strange                   in-degree = 50\n",
      "  Deadpool                         in-degree = 33\n",
      "\n",
      "Top 5 by out-degree (links out the most — 'a list'):\n",
      "  Betsy Braddock                   out-degree = 28\n",
      "  Cloak and Dagger (characters)    out-degree = 24\n",
      "  Adam Warlock                     out-degree = 22\n",
      "  Venom (character)                out-degree = 21\n",
      "  She-Hulk                         out-degree = 20\n",
